  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.3.15 - Auto-rigging: SkinTokensRigger gives a generated character a skeleton and learned skin weights in one pass (VAST AI SkinTokens, MIT, re-implemented on ILGPU; 5.8 s on CUDA, runs in the browser on WebGPU; 295/296 tokens identical to the PyTorch reference, skin weights 5.7e-5), UniRigRigger is the smaller skeleton + skinning-prior alternative, and the Image to 3D demo has a Rig this model button. v5.3.14 - TRELLIS.2 meshes are cleaned up before they are simplified and unwrapped (MeshRepair, on by default: non-manifold edges, winding, small holes, floating fragments). v5.3.13 -Browser storage is not capped at 10 GB: Chrome's navigator.storage.estimate() reports usage + 10 GiB, not a limit (BrowserStorageEstimate, RangeStreamModelSource plans every file for the cache and falls back to streaming only when the browser really refuses a write). v5.3.12 -SentencePiece honours the GGUF tokenizer.ggml.add_space_prefix flag (Gemma 2/3 multi-turn chat fixed: no stray space token at turn boundaries). v5.3.11 -Image and text to 3D (TRELLIS.2: photo or prompt -> PBR GLB) on CUDA (tensor cores), OpenCL, CPU and in the browser on WebGPU (portable tiled GEMM + flash attention, device mesh clustering, checkpoint streaming / per-file OPFS caching, background pipeline builds). Face detection and recognition (YuNet + SFace, matched against OpenCV). Requires SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.3.8. See CHANGELOG.md.",
